WEBVTT

00:00:28.874 --> 00:00:30.494
you might look up at the night sky

00:00:30.518 --> 00:00:32.070
and trust what you see.

00:00:32.094 --> 00:00:33.404
That's what Aristotle,

00:00:33.428 --> 00:00:35.854
THE guy to ask back then, did.

00:00:35.878 --> 00:00:38.212
He thought that since we're
on Earth, looking up,

00:00:38.236 --> 00:00:40.032
it must be the center, right?

00:00:40.056 --> 00:00:41.876
For him, the sphere of the world

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:43.630
was made up of four elements:

00:00:43.654 --> 00:00:44.045
Earth,

00:00:44.069 --> 00:00:44.497
water,

00:00:44.521 --> 00:00:44.964
air,

00:00:44.988 --> 00:00:46.165
and fire.

00:00:46.189 --> 00:00:48.417
These elements shifted around a nested set

00:00:48.441 --> 00:00:50.779
of solid crystalline spheres.

00:00:50.803 --> 00:00:53.298
Each of the wandering stars, the planets,

00:00:53.322 --> 00:00:55.175
had their own crystal sphere.

00:00:55.199 --> 00:00:57.636
The rest of the universe
and all of its stars

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:59.845
were on the last crystal sphere.

00:00:59.869 --> 00:01:01.764
If you watch the sky change over time,